&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW104639616 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW104639616 BCX0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;250&quot;&gt;Start:&lt;/strong&gt; 01.01.2027&amp;nbsp;| Level: Lead | Location: Germany, remote | Working hours: Fulltime (40h/week)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Master Data Management Lead, you will bear overall strategic responsibility for master data management across the entire company. In this role, you will define the governance structure, set priorities for MDM initiatives, and ensure that data ownership, decision-making rights, and processes are clearly established. You will act as the central interface between business strategy and operational data.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role can be performed remotely from anywhere within Germany, with occasional visits to our headquarters in Hamburg (approximately once per month during the first year, with less frequent visits possible thereafter)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot;&gt;You are responsible for the global MDM strategy, the roadmap, and the data governance framework, as well as defining clear data responsibilities (Data Ownership)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot;&gt;You will build a central MDM Center of Competence (CoC) within the TQG Group, establish standards, and ensure the internal development of expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot;&gt;You will lead the MDM team functionally and disciplinary, and coordinate the Business and Technical Data Stewards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot;&gt;You will design the Master Data Operating Model (MDOM) as well as end-to-end, cross-domain master data processes (Product, Customer, Supplier, Finance, Logistics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot;&gt;You will act as a bridge to the business units (SCM, Sales, Finance, etc.) and lead strategic governance committees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,5,0&quot;&gt;You will define and monitor MDM metrics (KPIs) using dashboards and drive continuous improvement processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,6,0&quot;&gt;You will work closely with the MDM data architecture team to optimally translate strategic guidelines into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;7,6,0&quot;&gt;You will actively promote a cultural shift toward active data ownership across the entire organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your experience &amp;amp; skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot;&gt;You bring at least 7 years of profound professional experience in the field of MDM, data governance, or data-driven transformation projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot;&gt;Ideally, you possess solid industry expertise in FMCG, food, dietary supplements, or retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot;&gt;You have proven leadership competence in cross-departmental projects as well as experience in building MDM governance structures in medium-sized companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,3,0&quot;&gt;You understand end-to-end master data processes (especially Product, Customer, Supplier, and Finance) down to the smallest detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,4,0&quot;&gt;You have sound knowledge of SAP S/4HANA within the master data context and are familiar with systems such as ERP, PIM (e.g., Akeneo), CRM, WMS, or PLM (e.g., Centric)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,5,0&quot;&gt;You possess practical know-how regarding data models and system integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,6,0&quot;&gt;You are characterized by a structured, analytical, and strategic mindset, paired with a documentation quality suitable for top-management level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;10,7,0&quot;&gt;You convince with strong communication and moderation skills to drive organizational change, and you are fluent in both German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why choose us?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being part of our team means joining a high-performing company with a diverse and inclusive culture. In our fast-growing team of over 1,200 employees, we combine our passion for sports nutrition, supplements, and healthy foods with cutting-edge technology, production, and logistics processes. All of this serves one goal: providing our customers with top-quality products to support their healthy and active lifestyle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can look forward to a strong sense of team spirit, ongoing opportunities for professional growth and responsibility, and an exciting work environment that blends lifestyle and career. With locations in Hamburg, Elmshorn, Kaltenkirchen/Nützen, and Elsdorf, TQG offers diverse career opportunities in areas such as technology, product development, sales, marketing, and logistics. Additionally, you’ll benefit from:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours and remote work options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive employee discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidy for the E-gym Wellpass&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 days vacation/year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and much more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quality Group (TQG) is an innovative provider of sports nutrition products, bringing together the successful brands&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;ESN&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;More Nutrition&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;since 2021.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ESN&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;has been the German market leader in sports nutrition since 2004, offering products like protein powders, bars, and supplements designed for ambitious fitness goals. Founded in 2017,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;More Nutrition&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;focuses on healthy, reduced-sugar foods, providing solutions for conscious nutrition and weight management without compromise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TQG’s vision is to help people become the best version of themselves. With passion and innovation, the company develops high-quality products that promote health, performance, and joy in life. Its agile company culture and exciting career opportunities make TQG a strong partner not only for customers but also for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is us – The Quality Group – nice to meet you! Now it’s your turn!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We look forward to your application! Regardless of gender, age, background, or identity – what matters to us is who you are and what you bring to the table. Join our team and grow with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the product agenda for how AI creates real, measurable value across Awin — translating AI capability into shipped product outcomes, not experiments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Thousands of advertisers and publishers who stay on Awin platform because of the people and product behind the service. The next chapter of Awin&#39;s product strategy is defined by how deliberately we put AI to work — not as a slogan, but as a set of practical capabilities embedded into what we build and how the business runs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Most companies treat AI as a layer bolted onto existing product thinking. We want the opposite: a Head of Product who treats AI as core to the product strategy itself — where it belongs, what it should never touch, and how it compounds value over time rather than producing one-off wins.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;3&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Product strategy for AI-driven value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Define where AI genuinely changes the economics or experience of our product — and where it doesn&#39;t. Prioritise like a product leader: value creation and value capture, not novelty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
